(LAN) Local Area Network - Connected devices in the same building or area

(WAN) Wide Area Network - Connected across large distances

(PAN) Personal Area Network - Connect personal devices within immediate space 
ex; bluetooth

(TCP/IP) Transmission Control Protocol/Internet Protocol - Communication protocols used to connect devices and route data
across the internet and private neworks 

(TCP) Transmission Control Protocol - Breaks data into packets , tracks them during transmission, ensures they are not 
corrupted, and reassembles at the destination

(IP) Internet Protocol - Ensures data packets know exactly where they are going 

3 Way Handshake: SYN - Open a connection
                 FIN - closes a connection
                 ACK - acknowledges a SYN or FIN


 computer               SYN                server
-----------    ---------------------->   -----------
|         |           SYN/ACK            |         |
|         |    <----------------------   |         |
|         |             ACK              |         |
-----------    --------------------- >   -----------

(UDP) User Datagram Protocol - Fast, lightweight protocol that sends data directly to a destination without establishing 
a connection 
ex; Streaming 

*OSI MODEL

1. Physical Layer:  Wires, Radios, Optics

2. Data Link Layer: Data Transfers between two nodes

3. Network Layer:   Internet Protocol (IP)

4. Transport Layer: TCP and UDP

5. Session Layer:   Exchanges between systems

6. Presentation Layer: Data Translation and encryption

7. Application Layer:  User Programs


*TCP Model

1. Network Interface Layer

2. Internet Layer 

3. Transport Layer 

4. Application Layer


*IP ADDRESS/DHCP

IP Address - Number identifier assigned to every device connected to a computer network
ex; 192.168.1.100

IPv4 - 32 bit
IPv6 - 128 bit

Static IPs - Manually assigned IP address that never changes

(DHCP) Dynamic Host Configuration Protocol- Auto assigns IP Addresses to devices connecting to a network

*Network Ports - Virtual doors on a computer that allow different programs to send and receive data over the internet

(Analogy)  Computer:     Apartment Building
           Application:  Apartment Unit
           IP Address:   Apartment Address
           Network Port: Apartment Number 

